        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 120,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: To have \\(AB\\) and \\(CD\\) intersect, the points must be arranged such that one pair of points (say \\(A\\) and \\(B\\)) separates the other pair (say \\(C\\) and \\(D\\)). This means if we list the points in order around the circle, the points must alternate between the two pairs."
      },
      {
