        "char_start": 461,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 212,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 213,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Calculate the total number of ways to arrange the four points \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(C\\), and \\(D\\) around the circle. Since the points are distinct and the circle is symmetric, we can fix one point (say \\(A\\)) and arrange the remaining three points in \\(3!\\) (3 factorial) ways. Therefore, there are \\(3! = 6\\) ways to arrange the remaining three points."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1015,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1017,
